meta {
  name: Rewrite Template For Utility
  type: graphql
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{api_url}}
  body: graphql
  auth: none
}

headers {
  authorization: {{auth_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:graphql {
  mutation rewriteTemplateForUtility($body: String!, $footer: String, $buttons: [String], $label: String) {
    rewriteTemplateForUtility(body: $body, footer: $footer, buttons: $buttons, label: $label) {
      body
      suggestedCategory
      changes {
        whatChanged
        why
        bestPractice
        bestPracticeUrl
      }
      errors {
        key
        message
      }
    }
  }
}

body:graphql:vars {
  {
    "body": "Hi {{1}}, don't miss our exciting new event this weekend!!",
    "footer": "Reply STOP to opt out",
    "buttons": ["Confirm"],
    "label": "Event reminder"
  }
}

docs {
  # Rewrite Template For Utility

  ## Description
  Rewrites a draft WhatsApp HSM template's body via Glific's AI runtime so it is eligible for
  Meta's UTILITY template category, and explains what was changed and why. Draft/create-flow
  tooling only — it never reads or writes a `SessionTemplate` row, and does not touch buttons or
  footer, only `body`.

  Requires the `staff` role or above, and the `is_template_utility_rewrite_enabled` feature flag
  to be on for the organization.

  ## Base URL
  `{{api_url}}`

  ## Parameters
  | Parameter | Description                                                        |
  |-----------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | `body`    | Required. The current draft body, including any `{{n}}` variables.  |
  | `footer`  | Optional. The current draft footer — used to check the combined character budget, never rewritten. |
  | `buttons` | Optional. The current draft's button text — used to check the combined character budget, never rewritten. |
  | `label`   | Optional. The draft's internal label, for context only.             |

  ## Request Example
  ```bash
  curl -X POST {{api_url}} \
      -H "Authorization: {{auth_token}}" \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d '{
          "query": "mutation rewriteTemplateForUtility($body: String!, $footer: String, $buttons: [String], $label: String) { rewriteTemplateForUtility(body: $body, footer: $footer, buttons: $buttons, label: $label) { body suggestedCategory changes { whatChanged why bestPractice bestPracticeUrl } errors { key message } } }",
          "variables": {
              "body": "Hi {{1}}, don'\''t miss our exciting new event this weekend!!",
              "footer": "Reply STOP to opt out",
              "buttons": ["Confirm"],
              "label": "Event reminder"
          }
      }'
  ```

  ## Response
  A successful rewrite:
  ```json
  {
    "data": {
      "rewriteTemplateForUtility": {
        "body": "Hi {{1}}, your event registration is confirmed.",
        "suggestedCategory": "UTILITY",
        "changes": [
          {
            "whatChanged": "Removed the promotional call-to-action and exclamation marks",
            "why": "Utility templates should confirm something the recipient already did, not invite them to something new",
            "bestPractice": "Avoid urgency and hype in utility copy",
            "bestPracticeUrl": null
          }
        ],
        "errors": []
      }
    }
  }
  ```

  A rewrite that fails one of the hard checks the backend enforces (the same `{{n}}` variables
  preserved in order, the body + buttons + footer combined 1024-character budget, or
  `suggestedCategory` being a recognised category) comes back as a field-level entry in
  `errors`, not a top-level GraphQL error, so the body/category/changes fields are all `null`:
  ```json
  {
    "data": {
      "rewriteTemplateForUtility": {
        "body": null,
        "suggestedCategory": null,
        "changes": null,
        "errors": [
          {
            "key": "body",
            "message": "The rewritten body must keep exactly the same {{n}} placeholders, in the same count and order, as the original body."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
  ```

  A feature-flag-off organization, or a caller below the `staff` role, gets a top-level GraphQL
  error instead — the same as every other `Authorize`/`RequireFeatureFlag`-gated field in this
  API:
  ```json
  {
    "data": { "rewriteTemplateForUtility": null },
    "errors": [
      { "message": "Template Utility Rewrite is not enabled for the organization." }
    ]
  }
  ```

  ## Use Cases
  1. **Use Case 1: Convert a marketing-styled draft to UTILITY.** Staff drafting an HSM notices
     it reads promotionally and wants it reworded to qualify for the cheaper, higher-throughput
     UTILITY category before submitting it for BSP approval.

  ## FAQ
  None
}
